                        "source_sense_id": "5b608c53-4198-3fda-af8c-b64870e18f1f",
                        "target_lang_word": "teddy bear",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "teddy bear",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5cf210e3-1ed2-3436-9ad7-cb239249e96f",
                                        "entry_id": "233337b9-f181-3d89-9715-4707977bb5e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plush toy in the shape of a bear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "447e4eba-3d78-4122-8120-3678d5b355d7",
                                                "sense_id": "5cf210e3-1ed2-3436-9ad7-cb239249e96f",
                                                "text": "1988, Michael Weikath, \"Rise and Fall\", Helloween, Keeper of the Seven Keys: Part II.\nThe king of Los Angeles / Bought himself a teddy bear / And the queen became shameless / She did it with a chair"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f80d31e-b7c7-4344-86b6-47c85ce25200",
                                                "sense_id": "5cf210e3-1ed2-3436-9ad7-cb239249e96f",
                                                "text": "The origin of Paddington (the bear, not the station) dates to 1956 when author Michael Bond (1926-2017) spotted a lonesome teddy bear on the shelf of a store near the station. It was Christmas Eve, so he bought the solitary bear for his wife."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d1c5fd1-a31a-3c11-890f-83665e971756",
                                        "entry_id": "233337b9-f181-3d89-9715-4707977bb5e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lovable, endearing, large, strong, hairy, or sweet man, particularly one who is gentle in spite of a burly or gruff appearance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56c46c69-02ad-4cfd-88de-1a3d14fd436f",
                                                "sense_id": "1d1c5fd1-a31a-3c11-890f-83665e971756",
                                                "text": "I'd like to mt you if you're a bearded ‘Teddy Bear,’ husky build, under 34 & share a career orientation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74a58d79-1e27-4515-a33b-a3aef43a55ad",
                                                "sense_id": "1d1c5fd1-a31a-3c11-890f-83665e971756",
                                                "text": "...the sexy \"teddy bear\" frontman of the '80s rap group Heavy D and the Boyz."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11ed3a62-6c2a-4d78-8172-04db151ff5f9",
                                                "sense_id": "1d1c5fd1-a31a-3c11-890f-83665e971756",
                                                "text": "This is not to say that women don't admire the Brad Pitts and George Clooneys of the world, but they're just as likely to be attracted to a big, teddy bear kind of man as the guy gracing the cover of GQ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "126d1d39-8d3e-4ec4-ad1b-5921d8d1f20b",
                                                "sense_id": "1d1c5fd1-a31a-3c11-890f-83665e971756",
                                                "text": "Some insisted that, because men have generally hairier bodies than women, a super-hairy chest is super-male and therefore very appealing. They added that it not only looks sexy but also feels sexy, like a teddy bear."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "150cdb8c-138e-412e-8735-52ff4df8600c",
                                                "sense_id": "1d1c5fd1-a31a-3c11-890f-83665e971756",
                                                "text": "“So I'm sort of a big teddy bear, am I?” “A sexy teddy bear.” he kissed her neck."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
